---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Genestealer Cults Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Genestealer Cults? Learn how Cult Ambush works, how to paint two-tone hybrid skin, and exactly what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🧬</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Genestealer Cults</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            The insurgents hiding in plain sight. Generations of hybrid cultists have infiltrated 
            every level of Imperial society, waiting for the signal. When it comes, they rise 
            as one — from within, just as the fleet strikes from without.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Ambush Insurgents</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-green-400">Easy–Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Hard</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-3 italic">*The Cult Ambush mechanic is this army's identity. Complex to learn, devastating to master. Not recommended as a first army.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">The rising</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          It begins with a single infected host. A Genestealer Patriarch — a monstrous, 
          psychically powerful alien creature — arrives on a world and bites a single human. 
          That human doesn't die. Instead, they become infected with genestealer DNA, 
          compelled by the Patriarch's will, and driven to spread the infection through 
          their family. Their children are hybrids. Their grandchildren more so. 
          By the fourth generation, some look almost human.
        </p>
        <p>
          Across decades, sometimes centuries, the cult grows. Its members infiltrate 
          the mines, the factorums, the Planetary Defense Force, the local Administratum. 
          They appear loyal citizens. They work. They worship. They wait. The Patriarch 
          sits at the center of a psychic web, sensing everything its progeny sense, 
          directing everything through a compulsion the hybrids feel as devotion.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then the Tyranid Hive Fleet appears on the edge of the system, and the signal goes out. 
          Every cultist, every hybrid, every mutant with even a drop of genestealer blood rises 
          simultaneously. They don't fight for conquest. They fight because the Patriarch's 
          genetic imprint drives them toward the Great Devourer. They are the galaxy's 
          most patient weapon — and they've already won before the shooting starts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Genestealer Cults' defining ability is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Cult Ambush</strong> — 
          units can be held in reserve and deployed mid-battle anywhere on the table, 
          including directly behind enemy lines or emerging from beneath enemy units. 
          The army fights like a trap: you set it up over the first turns, then spring it 
          all at once when the moment is right.
        </p>
        <p>
          Different unit types serve different roles in the ambush. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Neophyte Hybrids</strong> (the human-looking ones) 
          hold objectives and provide cheap board presence. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Acolyte Hybrids</strong> are your assault troops — 
          more alien, with claw arms, coming in from reserve to charge. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Aberrants</strong> are enormous, mutated brutes who 
          smash things in melee. The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Goliath Rockgrinder</strong> 
          is a mining vehicle turned battering ram.
        </p>
        <p>
          The cognitive demand is real: planning where your reserve units will appear 
          requires reading three or four turns ahead. If you spring the ambush too early, 
          your fragile units get shot off the table before they can act. Too late, 
          and the game is lost. When it works, it's the most satisfying army in 40k.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">GSC are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You love strategic planning and setting traps</li>
            <li>✓ The body horror insurgent aesthetic appeals to you</li>
            <li>✓ You want a faction almost nobody else plays</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy a high model count army</li>
            <li>✓ The challenge of a complex army excites you</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You're still learning 40k fundamentals</li>
            <li>✗ You want a forgiving, durable army</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer straightforward game plans</li>
            <li>✗ You don't want to track many reserve units</li>
            <li>✗ You want strong shooting at long range</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cult Ambush explained -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">The Cult Ambush mechanic</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        This is the army's identity. Everything else is secondary. Understanding this is 
        understanding Genestealer Cults.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-8">
        {[
          {
            label: 'Setup',
            title: 'Before the game',
            desc: 'You designate which units will deploy normally and which will be held in Cult Ambush (reserve). Neophytes often deploy on the table for early objective control. Your assault units — Acolytes, Aberrants — often start in reserve.',
          },
          {
            label: 'Infiltration',
            title: 'Turns 1–2',
            desc: 'Your on-table units move to control ground and threaten the opponent. You\'re reading where they\'re committing their forces, where the gaps are, and where your ambushing units will appear for maximum impact.',
          },
          {
            label: 'The Spring',
            title: 'When the moment is right',
            desc: 'Reserve units appear mid-battle — from any board edge, from designated ambush points, or via special abilities, from directly next to or beneath enemy units. Multiple squads materialise in one turn, surrounding the opponent from angles they weren\'t watching.',
          },
          {
            label: 'The Decisive Turn',
            title: 'The assault',
            desc: 'Acolytes charge. Aberrants smash. The Rockgrinder rams. If you\'ve timed it correctly, the opponent has no good answer because the threat came from every direction at once. This is the moment the whole army is built around.',
          },
        ].map(step => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-2">
              <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display">{step.label}</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold">{step.title}</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{step.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm italic">
        The trap only works if you've read the game state correctly. Against an experienced opponent, 
        a mistimed ambush can cost you the game in one turn. The ceiling for mastery is extremely high — 
        but so is the payoff.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Genestealer Cults</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        The distinctive look is two-tone skin — human flesh blending into alien purple — 
        plus industrial workwear. Easier than it looks, and incredibly striking at army scale.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Prime grey, base coat clothing</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Grey Seer spray primer (ideal for both skin tones and clothing). Base coat overalls and work gear in your chosen cult color — Mechanicus Standard Grey for industrial grey, Zandri Dust for a miner's brown, or a bright color if you want a vibrant cult identity.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Human skin zones — Rakarth Flesh</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Paint the more human areas of skin (faces, necks, hands on lower-generation hybrids) with Rakarth Flesh. This is your warm, human tone. Apply Reikland Fleshshade into the recesses, then re-highlight with Pallid Wych Flesh.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Alien skin zones — Warpfiend Grey or Genestealer Purple</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The more alien areas (scalps on Acolytes, extra limbs, the Patriarch's head) take Genestealer Purple or Warpfiend Grey. Shade with Druchii Violet. Highlight back up with Slaanesh Grey. Where the two skin tones meet, blend them together on higher-generation hybrids.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Industrial workwear — shade and highlight</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply Agrax Earthshade over all the clothing. Once dry, drybrush a lighter version of the base color back over the fabric for instant texture. Mining equipment and straps can pick up Leadbelcher for metallics.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Weapons and claws</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Improvised weapons (mining equipment, stubbers) in Leadbelcher → Nuln Oil. Alien rending claws: Ushabti Bone base → Agrax shade → Screaming Skull highlight with thin edge lines. Teeth and talons follow the same recipe.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Eyes — the most important detail</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Genestealer eyes are oval and alien. Mephiston Red with a tiny dot of Blood Angel Red Contrast works well. A single white highlight dot transforms them. Get these right on the characters — the Magus especially — and the whole army looks alive.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">Batch painting tip — the horde advantage</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          You have 20 Neophytes in the Combat Patrol alone. 
          Batch paint them in groups of 5: all skin step 1 across all 5, then all skin step 2, and so on. 
          The two-tone skin looks complex but is actually fast once you're in a rhythm. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Contrast paints are your friend here</strong> — 
          Guilliman Flesh + Shyish Purple does both skin tones quickly on a Wraithbone prime.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol. It contains the core unit types you need to learn the Cult Ambush mechanic properly.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Genestealer Cults</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes a Magus (psyker leader), a Goliath Rockgrinder, 5 Aberrants, 
          5 Acolyte Hybrids (or Hybrid Metamorphs), and 20 Neophyte Hybrids — 
          32 models total. Every unit type you need to learn the army. 
          The Neophyte horde alone teaches you how the army occupies the table.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D63C96WS?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$55 · first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">A second Neophyte Hybrids box</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          More Neophytes means more objective holders, more screening units, and more 
          bodies to sacrifice while your ambush units wait in reserve. 
          You almost always want more Neophytes in a Cult list.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=neophyte+hybrids+genestealer+cults+warhammer&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Grey Seer Spray', use: 'Primer — works for both skin tones', required: true },
            { name: 'Rakarth Flesh', use: 'Human skin base coat', required: true },
            { name: 'Reikland Fleshshade', use: 'Shade for human flesh zones', required: true },
            { name: 'Genestealer Purple', use: 'Alien skin base coat', required: true },
            { name: 'Druchii Violet', use: 'Shade for alien skin zones', required: true },
            { name: 'Agrax Earthshade', use: 'Shade for clothing and equipment', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Mining equipment and weapons', required: true },
            { name: 'Ushabti Bone', use: 'Claws, teeth, alien talons', required: false },
            { name: 'Mechanicus Standard Grey', use: 'Industrial clothing base coat', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">Painting 32 models sounds daunting. Use batch painting and Contrast paints — it goes faster than you think.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Genestealer Cults', cost: '~$160', note: '32 models — strong patrol army' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (7)', cost: '~$42', note: 'Two-tone skin + clothing + metals' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Industrial rubble or texture paint' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Lots of small alien arms to attach' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$239</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Good value per model — the Combat Patrol contains 32 models including a vehicle. 
        Genestealer Cults scale up affordably because Neophytes come in large cheap boxes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">The signal goes out. They rise.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Patience is the cult's weapon. Learn the ambush mechanic, learn to read the game state, 
        and spring the trap at the exact right moment. The galaxy never sees it coming until it's too late.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
